se apply_patch. Read docs/conventions/authoring.md. Repo uses vp. Run focused guard tests if feasible. Do not commit or update snapshot. Return edited paths and explicit coverage decisions. Do not delegate. User approved all five phases; others own other records. Ignore unrelated dirty l10n/docs.api.pot.\"}\n[tool task -> success] args={\"description\":\"Expand color audit fixtures\",\"agent_type\":\"general-purpose\",\"mode\":\"background\",\"name\":\"color-fixtures\",\"prompt\":\"Implement phase 2 only: expand -automatica11y examples for core components button,alert,badge,pill,avatar,text,heading,progress,progress-circle,view,link,close-button,spinner,card,context-view. Own ONLY their source dirs under formats/components/src/components (if record lives elsewhere inspect exact registry and edit only its source). Inspect actual CSS/metadata before edit. Cover all distinct supported colors/sizes/states, dedup aliases; one audit example per record with all variants. Use realistic valid required semantics and minimal owned content, no unrelated components. Inverse/on-color variants require correct contrasting surface, not inline overrides of tested color; inspect tokens/available surface utilities. Keep docs/Canvas examples and runtime CSS unchanged. Don't hide failures or drop difficult variants. Avoid manufacturing reflow from wide fixture layouts. Use apply_patch, follow docs/conventions/authoring.md. Run guard tests if feasible. No commits/snapshot changes. Return paths and coverage decisions. Do not delegate. Other agents own forms/size/plugins; ignore unrelated worktree changes.\"}\n[tool task -> success] args={\"description\":\"Expand structural audit fixtures\",\"agent_type\":\"general-purpose\",\"mode\":\"background\",\"name\":\"structural-fixtures\",\"prompt\":\"Implement phases 3 and core portion of 5: inspect and strengthen all remaining core component audit examples EXCLUDING color agent owned button,alert,badge,pill,avatar,text,heading,progress,progress-circle,view,link,close-button,spinner,card,context-view and forms agent owned text-input,text-area,simple-select,input-group,number-input,checkbox,radio,tag,form-field,form-field-group,radio-input-group,form-field-messages,in-place-edit,file-drop,range-input. Your scope includes list,breadcrumb,byline,img,metric,rating,toggle-group,tree-browser,tray,modal and members,tabs and members,calendar and member,pagination and member,drawer-layout and members,menu and members,table and members,toggle-details,popover,tooltip,side-nav-bar and members,mask. Inspect registries to locate actual sources. Cover distinct supported color/size/state variants dedup aliases, one -automatica11y example per record with all variants. Required parent/member markup stays, unrelated slotted components go; preserve valid names/IDs/semantics and behavior wiring. Do not edit runtime CSS or docs/Canvas examples. No manufactured reflow layouts, don't hide genuine failures. Use apply_patch, follow docs/conventions/authoring.md. No commits or snapshot updates. Run guard tests if feasible. Return edited paths and explicit decisions for records needing no change. Do not delegate. Other agents editing disjoint dirs; ignore their changes.\"}\n[tool view -> success] args={\"path\":\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/plugins/pantoken/custom-components/src/components/banner/banner.css\",\"view_range\":[1,165]}\n[tool view -> success] args={\"path\":\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/plugins/pantoken/custom-components/src/components/button-set/button-set.css\",\"view_range\":[1,180]}\n[tool view -> success] args={\"path\":\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/plugins/pantoken/custom-components/src/components/segmented-control/segmented-control.css\",\"view_range\":[1,160]}\n[tool view -> success] args={\"path\":\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/plugins/pantoken/custom-components/src/components/skeleton-loader/skeleton-loader.css\",\"view_range\":[1,150]}\n[tool view -> success] args={\"path\":\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoke