{"type":"permission.requested","data":{"requestId":"26be42b2-672d-4c34-a669-02fdc05e7a74","permissionRequest":{"kind":"write","toolCallId":"custom_call_2vGqbMGQH3tDBqViVLzZvwhQ","intention":"Update file","fileName":"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/list/list.css","diff":"\ndiff --git a/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/list/list.css b/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/list/list.css\nindex 0000000..0000000 100644\n--- a/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/list/list.css\n+++ b/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/list/list.css\n@@ -23,11 +23,11 @@\n  * ```\n  * @example -automatica11y\n  * ```html\n- * <ul class=\"pfx-list\">\n- *   <li>First item</li>\n- *   <li>Second item</li>\n- *   <li>Third item</li>\n- * </ul>\n+ * <ul class=\"pfx-list -size-sm\"><li>Small first item</li><li>Small second item</li></ul>\n+ * <ul class=\"pfx-list -size-md\"><li>Medium first item</li><li>Medium second item</li></ul>\n+ * <ul class=\"pfx-list -size-lg\"><li>Large first item</li><li>Large second item</li></ul>\n+ * <ul class=\"pfx-list -unstyled\" role=\"list\"><li>Unstyled first item</li><li>Unstyled second item</li></ul>\n+ * <ul class=\"pfx-list -inline\" role=\"list\"><li>Inline first item</li><li>Inline second item</li></ul>\n  * ```\n  */\n @scope (.pfx-list) {\n","newFileContents":"/**\n * @component list\n * @selector .pfx-list\n * @a11y Use a real `<ul>` or `<ol>` with `<li>` children. Removing markers with `-unstyled` can make some screen readers drop the list semantics, so add `role=\"list\"` when the list structure matters.\n * @summary A list with token-driven item spacing.\n * @remarks Sets its own `padding-inline-start` for list indentation; chaining a `-p*`/`-padding*` spacing utility modifier overrides that built-in value. See the `list.item` member for the individual items.\n * @modifier -inline — Lay items out inline (horizontal).\n * @modifier -unstyled — Remove markers and padding.\n * @modifier -size-sm — Small. @affects list.item — Scales the item spacing to match.\n * @modifier -size-md — Medium (default). @affects list.item — Scales the item spacing to match.\n * @modifier -size-lg — Large. @affects list.item — Scales the item spacing to match.\n * @structure\n * .pfx-list {\n *   li:many {}\n * }\n * @example -canvas-rce -docs\n * ```html\n * <ul class=\"pfx-list\">\n *   <li>First item</li>\n *   <li>Second item</li>\n *   <li>Third item</li>\n * </ul>\n * ```\n * @example -automatica11y\n * ```html\n * <ul class=\"pfx-list -size-sm\"><li>Small first item</li><li>Small second item</li></ul>\n * <ul class=\"pfx-list -size-md\"><li>Medium first item</li><li>Medium second item</li></ul>\n * <ul class=\"pfx-list -size-lg\"><li>Large first item</li><li>Large second item</li></ul>\n * <ul class=\"pfx-list -unstyled\" role=\"list\"><li>Unstyled first item</li><li>Unstyled second item</li></ul>\n * <ul class=\"pfx-list -inline\" role=\"list\"><li>Inline first item</li><li>Inline second item</li></ul>\n * ```\n */\n@scope (.pfx-list) {\n  & {\n    color: var(--instui-component-list-item-color);\n    font-family: var(--instui-component-list-item-font-family);\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-list-item-font-size-medium);\n    font-weight: var(--instui-component-list-item-font-weight);\n    line-height: var(--instui-component-list-item-line-height);\n    padding-inline-start: var(--instui-component-list-list-padding);\n  }\n\n  &.-size-sm {\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-list-item-font-size-small);\n  }\n\n  &.-size-md {\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-list-item-font-size-medium);\n  }\n\n  &.-size-lg {\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-list-item-font-size-large);\n  }\n\n  /* isUnstyled: strip markers and indentation. */\n  &.-unstyled {\n    list-style: none;\n    padding-inline-start: 0;\n  }\n\n  /* InlineList: lay items out in a wrapping row (`.pfx-list.-inline`). */\n  &.-inline {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: var(--instui-component-list-item-spacing-medium);\n    list-style: none;\n    padding-inline-start: 0;\n  }\n\n  &.-inline > li {\n    margin: 0;\n  }\n}\n","canOfferSessionApproval":true,"fileEdits":[{"before":{"path":"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/list/list.css","content":"/**\n * @component list\n * @selector .pfx-list\n * @a11y Use a real `<ul>` or `<ol>` with `<li>` children. Removing markers with `-unstyled` can make some screen readers drop the list semantics, so add `role=\"list\"` when the list structure matters.\n * @summary A list with token-driven item spacing.\n * @remarks Sets its own `padding-inline-start` for list indentation; chaining a `-p*`/`-padding*` spacing utility modifier overrides that built-in value. See the `list.item` member for the individual items.\n * @modifier -inline — Lay items out inline (horizontal).\n * @modifier -unstyled — Remove markers and padding.\n * @modifier -size-sm — Small. @affects list.item — Scales the item spacing to match.\n * @modifier -size-md — Medium (default). @affects list.item — Scales the item spacing to match.\n * @modifier -size-lg — Large. @affects list.item — Scales the item spacing to match.\n * @structure\n * .pfx-list {\n *   li:many {}\n * }\n * @example -canvas-rce -docs\n * ```html\n * <ul class=\"pfx-list\">\n *   <li>First item</li>\n *   <li>Second item</li>\n *   <li>Third item</li>\n * </ul>\n * ```\n * @example -automatica11y\n * ```html\n * <ul class=\"pfx-list\">\n *   <li>First item</li>\n *   <li>Second item</li>\n *   <li>Third item</li>\n * </ul>\n * ```\n */\n@scope (.pfx-list) {\n  & {\n    color: var(--instui-component-list-item-color);\n    font-family: var(--instui-component-list-item-font-family);\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-list-item-font-size-medium);\n    font-weight: var(--instui-component-list-item-font-weight);\n    line-height: var(--instui-component-list-item-line-height);\n    padding-inline-start: var(--instui-component-list-list-padding);\n  }\n\n  &.-size-sm {\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-list-item-font-size-small);\n  }\n\n  &.-size-md {\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-list-item-font-size-medium);\n  }\n\n  &.-size-lg {\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-list-item-font-size-large);\n  }\n\n  /* isUnstyled: strip markers and indentation. */\n  &.-unstyled {\n    list-style: none;\n    padding-inline-start: 0;\n  }\n\n  /* InlineList: lay items out in a wrapping row (`.pfx-list.-inline`). */\n  &.-inline {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: var(--instui-component-list-item-spacing-medium);\n    list-style: none;\n    padding-inline-start: 0;\n  }\n\n  &.-inline > li {\n    margin: 0;\n  }\n}\n"},"after":{"path":"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/list/list.css","content":"/**\n * @component list\n * @selector .pfx-list\n * @a11y Use a real `<ul>` or `<ol>` with `<li>` children. Removing markers with `-unstyled` can make some screen readers drop the list semantics, so add `role=\"list\"` when the list structure matters.\n * @summary A list with token-driven item spacing.\n * @remarks Sets its own `padding-inline-start` for list indentation; chaining a `-p*`/`-padding*` spacing utility modifier overrides that built-in value. See the `list.item` member for the individual items.\n * @modifier -inline — Lay items out inline (horizontal).\n * @modifier -unstyled — Remove markers and padding.\n * @modifier -size-sm — Small. @affects list.item — Scales the item spacing to match.\n * @modifier -size-md — Medium (default). @affects list.item — Scales the item spacing to match.\n * @modifier -size-lg — Large. @affects list.item — Scales the item spacing to match.\n * @structure\n * .pfx-list {\n *   li:many {}\n * }\n * @example -canvas-rce -docs\n * ```html\n * <ul class=\"pfx-list\">\n *   <li>First ite