\": null,\\n  \\\"rawRequestKind\\\": \\\"write\\\",\\n  \\\"parsedCommandCount\\\": null,\\n  \\\"allParsedCommandsReadOnly\\\": null,\\n  \\\"hasWriteFileRedirection\\\": null,\\n  \\\"possiblePathCount\\\": null,\\n  \\\"possibleUrlCount\\\": null,\\n  \\\"requestSandboxBypass\\\": false\\n}\\n```\\n\\n`permissionBoundary` identifies what the permission engine is currently asking to approve. A `path` boundary means path access itself requires approval. A `commands` boundary means the permission engine did not require separate approval for the paths its heuristic extractor found; use that as strong scope evidence while still checking for visibly sensitive or unrelated paths. Parser booleans describe visible syntax only and do not prove that repository, package-manager, or user configuration cannot execute additional code.\\n\\nShell parsing and `scriptActionReview` describe available evidence, not a permission verdict. Missing source snapshots, dynamic expressions and incomplete parsing are uncertainties to assess with the full command and conversation, not automatic approval or rejection. Do not assume missing values or effects are harmless.\\n\\nProposed action (kind: write):\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"kind\\\": \\\"write\\\",\\n  \\\"toolCallId\\\": \\\"REDACTED\\\",\\n  \\\"intention\\\": \\\"Update file\\\",\\n  \\\"fileName\\\": \\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/in-place-edit/in-place-edit.css\\\",\\n  \\\"diff\\\": \\\"\\\\ndiff --git a/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/in-place-edit/in-place-edit.css b/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/in-place-edit/in-place-edit.css\\\\nindex 0000000..0000000 100644\\\\n--- a/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/in-place-edit/in-place-edit.css\\\\n+++ b/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/in-place-edit/in-place-edit.css\\\\n@@ -13,7 +13,8 @@\\\\n  * @demo self:in-place-edit\\\\n  * @example -automatica11y\\\\n  * ```html\\\\n- * <span class=\\\\\\\"pfx-in-place-edit\\\\\\\" contenteditable=\\\\\\\"true\\\\\\\" role=\\\\\\\"textbox\\\\\\\" aria-label=\\\\\\\"Project name\\\\\\\">Untitled</span>\\\\n+ * <p><span id=\\\\\\\"audit-project-label\\\\\\\">Project name</span>: <span class=\\\\\\\"pfx-in-place-edit\\\\\\\" contenteditable=\\\\\\\"true\\\\\\\" role=\\\\\\\"textbox\\\\\\\" aria-labelledby=\\\\\\\"audit-project-label\\\\\\\">Untitled</span></p>\\\\n+ * <p><span id=\\\\\\\"audit-project-locked-label\\\\\\\">Locked project name</span>: <span class=\\\\\\\"pfx-in-place-edit -readonly\\\\\\\" contenteditable=\\\\\\\"false\\\\\\\" role=\\\\\\\"textbox\\\\\\\" aria-readonly=\\\\\\\"true\\\\\\\" aria-labelledby=\\\\\\\"audit-project-locked-label\\\\\\\">Published project</span></p>\\\\n  * ```\\\\n  */\\\\n @scope (.pfx-in-place-edit) {\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"newFileContents\\\": \\\"/**\\\\n * @component in-place-edit\\\\n * @selector .pfx-in-place-edit\\\\n * @summary A [contenteditable] that reads as text until focused, then shows input chrome.\\\\n * @remarks The input chrome only appears while focused; `-readonly` suppresses both the hover and focus affordances so the element always reads as plain inline text.\\\\n * @modifier -readonly — Shown inline but not editable (no hover/focus affordance).\\\\n * @a11y Give the editable element `role=\\\\\\\"textbox\\\\\\\"` and an accessible name (`aria-label`).\\\\n * @example -canvas-rce -docs\\\\n * ```html\\\\n * <span class=\\\\\\\"pfx-in-place-edit\\\\\\\" contenteditable=\\\\\\\"true\\\\\\\" role=\\\\\\\"textbox\\\\\\\" aria-label=\\\\\\\"Project name\\\\\\\">Untitled</span>\\\\n * ```\\\\n * @related text-input — On focus it shows the same input chrome as a text input.\\\\n * @demo self:in-place-edit\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * ```html\\\\n * <p><span id=\\\\\\\"audit-project-label\\\\\\\">Project name</span>: <span class=\\\\\\\"pfx-in-place-edit\\\\\\\" contenteditable=\\\\\\\"true\\\\\