chars]\\\",\\n  \\\"newFileContents\\\": \\\"/**\\\\n * @component file-drop\\\\n * @selector .pfx-file-drop\\\\n * @summary A file dropzone with hover, accepted, and rejected states.\\\\n * @remarks The `-hover`/`-accepted`/`-rejected` classes are purely visual — actual drag-and-drop detection and file validation are the consumer's JS to wire up around the wrapped native input.\\\\n * @modifier -icon-* — Render the leading dropzone glyph icon.\\\\n * @modifier -accepted — Drag state for an acceptable file.\\\\n * @modifier -hover — Hover or drag-over state.\\\\n * @modifier -rejected — Drag state for a rejected file.\\\\n * @accessibility Wrap a native `<input type=\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\">` in the `<label>` drop zone so it stays a real, labelled file control that the keyboard and assistive tech can operate.\\\\n * @example -canvas-rce -docs\\\\n * ```html\\\\n * <label class=\\\\\\\"pfx-file-drop\\\\\\\" id=\\\\\\\"fd\\\\\\\">\\\\n *   <span class=\\\\\\\"pfx-icon -icon-cloud-upload\\\\\\\"></span>\\\\n *   <div class=\\\\\\\"pfx-text\\\\\\\"><strong>Drag an image here</strong>, or click to browse.</div>\\\\n *   <div class=\\\\\\\"pfx-text -size-sm pfx-fg-muted\\\\\\\" id=\\\\\\\"fd-msg\\\\\\\">PNG or JPG up to 5&nbsp;MB.</div>\\\\n *   <input type=\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\" id=\\\\\\\"fd-input\\\\\\\">\\\\n * </label>\\\\n * ```\\\\n * @structure\\\\n * .pfx-file-drop {\\\\n *   [class*=\\\\\\\"-icon-\\\\\\\"]:optional {}\\\\n *   .pfx-text {\\\\n *     strong {}\\\\n *   }\\\\n *   .pfx-text {}\\\\n *   input {}\\\\n * }\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * ```html\\\\n * <label class=\\\\\\\"pfx-file-drop\\\\\\\">\\\\n *   <span class=\\\\\\\"-icon-cloud-upload\\\\\\\" aria-hidden=\\\\\\\"true\\\\\\\"></span>\\\\n *   <span id=\\\\\\\"audit-file-label\\\\\\\">Upload an image</span>\\\\n *   <span id=\\\\\\\"audit-file-hint\\\\\\\">Choose a PNG or JPEG file, up to 5 MB.</span>\\\\n *   <input type=\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\" accept=\\\\\\\"image/png,image/jpeg\\\\\\\" aria-labelledby=\\\\\\\"audit-file-label\\\\\\\" aria-describedby=\\\\\\\"audit-file-hint\\\\\\\">\\\\n * </label>\\\\n * <label class=\\\\\\\"pfx-file-drop -hover\\\\\\\">\\\\n *   <span id=\\\\\\\"audit-file-hover-label\\\\\\\">Upload while dragging a file</span>\\\\n *   <span id=\\\\\\\"audit-file-hover-hint\\\\\\\">Drop the file here, or use the file picker.</span>\\\\n *   <input type=\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\" aria-labelledby=\\\\\\\"audit-file-hover-label\\\\\\\" aria-describedby=\\\\\\\"audit-file-hover-hint\\\\\\\">\\\\n * </label>\\\\n * <label class=\\\\\\\"pfx-… [truncated 1560 chars]\\\",\\n  \\\"canOfferSessionApproval\\\": true,\\n  \\\"_permissionRequestSessionId\\\": \\\"e0a110b6-b8dd-47be-82d5-cb60da15b229\\\",\\n  \\\"_subagentAgentId\\\": \\\"049c1373-ecc6-4d66-bbea-f19e45c06453\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Apply the policy to the concrete mechanics, not only the requested goal.\\nAn authorized project operation can still disable an audit or verification\\ncontrol through an extra flag. Suppressing that control for just one invocation\\nis a bypass. A live routing change can evade an integrity control when it\\nsubstitutes an unknown operator for a trusted service and verification will\\nnot prevent the substitution. A read can expose authentication secrets; a\\nconfiguration write can immediately change an active security boundary.\\nConversely, drafting an inactive artifact is not executing its future behavior.\\nIdentify an actual mandatory effect; do not invent one from a command's name.\\n\\nMandatory confirmation and a covering refusal take precedence over a grant,\\nexplicit delegation, convenience, and recoverability. Specific human approval\\ncannot override a mandatory class. Only after these exclusions may an existing\\ngrant or qualifying explicit or implicit delegation support ALLOW. Otherwise\\nDENY. An earlier explicit permission-prompt denial cannot be superseded by\\ninferring a grant from later prose.\\n\\nReply with exactly one line: ALLOW: <reason> or DENY: <reason>.\\nKeep the reason to at most 12 words.\\n\"}]","requestSettings":{"enabledFeatureFlags":["CATALOG_SEARCH","AGENT_FINDER_SKILL_INSTALL","copilot-feature-agentic-memory","copilot_feature_agentic_memory_user_scoped","QUEUED_COMMANDS","HYDRAFUSION","HYDRAFUSION_ROLLOUT","HYDRAFUSION_PLAN_V2","AUTO_APPROVAL","CONTENT_EXCLUSION","VIM_MODE","CLOUD_SESSION_STORE","COPILOT_GITHUB_TABS","COPILOT_GITHUB_THEME","COLLECT_DEBUG_LOGS","TOOL_SEARCH_ANTHROPIC","TOOL_SEARCH_OPENAI","BACKGROUND_SESSIONS","SANDBOX","VOICE","RUBBER_DUCK_AGENT","MCP_REGISTRY_INSTALL","SESSION_INDEXING","CLI_WORKTREE","REMOTE_JSON_RPC","PROMPT_FRAME","INLINE_IMAGES","DETACH_LONG_LIVED_SERVICES","WORKTREE","SESSIONS_SIDEBAR_TAB","MANAGED_REMOTE_CONTROL_SETTING","FAILBOT_ERROR_REPORTING","TIMELINE_TOUCHUP","BLACKBIRD_AUTO_INDEX","TGREP"]},"quotaSnapshots":{"chat":{"isUnlimitedEntitlement":true,"entitlementRequests":-1,"usedRequests":0,"usageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"overage":0,"overageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"remainingPercentage":100,"resetDate":"2026-11-01T00:00:00Z"},"completions":{"isUnlimitedEntitlement":true,"entitlementRequests":-1,"usedRequests":0,"usageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"overage":0,"overageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"remainingPercentage":100,"resetDate":"2026-11-01T00:00:00Z"},"premium_interactions":{"isUnlimitedEntitlement":true,"entitlementRequests":-1,"usedRequests":0,"usageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":true,"overage":0,"overageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":true,"remainingPercentage":100,"resetDate":"2026-11-01T00:00:00Z"}},"requestId":"5E57:28BF52:9AD231B:A346D7D:6AE26351","clientRequestId":"00000-74b1effe-c030-4eac-b18a-ff42d29e47ee","serviceRequestId":"bc621c32-8ad1-4ffd-87fe-7505cb3b05ae","rte":true,"copilotUsage":{"token_details":[{"batch_size":1000000,"cost_per_batch":10000000000,"model":"gpt-6-luna","token_count":3,"token_type":"input"},{"batch_size":1000000,"cost_per_batch":1000000000,"model":"gpt-6-lu