,\\\"13128f82-ab9e-41de-a14e-bd6978da289e\\\"],\\\"message\\\":\\\"Parsed CssDocEntry.modifiers carries modifier.alias.canonical (not description @alias) and modifier.pattern. I'll add metadata-derived guard that requires canonical visual color/size/variant/state modifier classes on matching component roots, skipping aliases/patterns. Flag any intentional exceptions with rationale. Please ensure data-a11y roots/triggers remain where harness needs them; root identifiers should remain unique. Guard tests now normalize pfx before checking IDs/ARIA for plugin records too.\\\"}\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"Runtime-derived request context:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"permissionBoundary\\\": \\\"write\\\",\\n  \\\"pathAccessKind\\\": null,\\n  \\\"rawRequestKind\\\": \\\"write\\\",\\n  \\\"parsedCommandCount\\\": null,\\n  \\\"allParsedCommandsReadOnly\\\": null,\\n  \\\"hasWriteFileRedirection\\\": null,\\n  \\\"possiblePathCount\\\": null,\\n  \\\"possibleUrlCount\\\": null,\\n  \\\"requestSandboxBypass\\\": false\\n}\\n```\\n\\n`permissionBoundary` identifies what the permission engine is currently asking to approve. A `path` boundary means path access itself requires approval. A `commands` boundary means the permission engine did not require separate approval for the paths its heuristic extractor found; use that as strong scope evidence while still checking for visibly sensitive or unrelated paths. Parser booleans describe visible syntax only and do not prove that repository, package-manager, or user configuration cannot execute additional code.\\n\\nShell parsing and `scriptActionReview` describe available evidence, not a permission verdict. Missing source snapshots, dynamic expressions and incomplete parsing are uncertainties to assess with the full command and conversation, not automatic approval or rejection. Do not assume missing values or effects are harmless.\\n\\nProposed action (kind: write):\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"kind\\\": \\\"write\\\",\\n  \\\"toolCallId\\\": \\\"REDACTED\\\",\\n  \\\"intention\\\": \\\"Update file\\\",\\n  \\\"fileName\\\": \\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/breadcrumb/members/link/link.css\\\",\\n  \\\"diff\\\": \\\"\\\\ndiff --git a/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/breadcrumb/members/link/link.css b/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/breadcrumb/members/link/link.css\\\\nindex 0000000..0000000 100644\\\\n--- a/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/breadcrumb/members/link/link.css\\\\n+++ b/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/breadcrumb/members/link/link.css\\\\n@@ -20,16 +20,9 @@\\\\n  * @stable\\\\n  * @example -automatica11y\\\\n  * ```html\\\\n- * <nav class=\\\\\\\"pfx-breadcrumb\\\\\\\" aria-label=\\\\\\\"Breadcrumb\\\\\\\">\\\\n- *   <ol>\\\\n- *     <li>\\\\n- *       <a class=\\\\\\\"-icon-house\\\\\\\" href=\\\\\\\"#\\\\\\\">Home</a>\\\\n- *     </li>\\\\n- *     <li><a href=\\\\\\\"#\\\\\\\">Guides</a></li>\\\\n- *     <li><a href=\\\\\\\"#\\\\\\\">Components</a></li>\\\\n- *     <li aria-current=\\\\\\\"page\\\\\\\">Breadcrumb</li>\\\\n- *   </ol>\\\\n- * </nav>\\\\n+ * <nav class=\\\\\\\"pfx-breadcrumb -size-sm\\\\\\\" aria-label=\\\\\\\"Small breadcrumb\\\\\\\"><ol><li><a href=\\\\\\\"#home\\\\\\\">Home</a></li><li aria-current=\\\\\\\"page\\\\\\\">Guides</li></ol></nav>\\\\n+ * <nav class=\\\\\\\"pfx-breadcrumb -size-md\\\\\\\" aria-label=\\\\\\\"Medium breadcrumb\\\\\\\"><ol><li><a href=\\\\\\\"#home\\\\\\\">Home</a></li><li aria-current=\\\\\\\"page\\\\\\\">Guides</li></ol></nav>\\\\n+ * <nav class=\\\\\\\"pfx-breadcrumb -size-lg\\\\\\\" aria-label=\\\\\\\"Large breadcrumb\\\\\\\"><ol><li><a href=\\\\\\\"#home\\\\\\\">Home</a></li><li aria-current=\\\\\\\"page\\\\\\\">Guides</li></ol></nav>\\\\n  * ```\\\\n  */\\\\n \\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"newFileContents\\\": \\\"/**\\\\n * @component breadcrumb.link\\\\n * @memberOf breadcrumb\\\\n * @selec