{"type":"model.message","data":{"kind":"message","turn":0,"modelCall":{"model":"gpt-6-luna","api_id":"","api_endpoint":"/responses","request_id":"5EEB:3AF051:957FF0D:9DFC318:6AE2635E","client_request_id":"00000-37cac905-6325-4702-8f43-083afbb3e752","service_request_id":"eee1eed1-cd36-4178-aa49-247ae3d2f1c2","rte":true,"initiator":"user","transport":"http"},"message":{"content":"ALLOW: Authorized audit-fixture expansion; no mandatory prohibited effect is present.","refusal":null,"role":"assistant","reasoning_opaque":"REDACTED","reasoning_text":"I need to evaluate the write expansion fixture based on the user's broad request for all components. There’s no mandatory effect, so that's a relief! The CSS document fixture is inert. I'll include an audit example data URI, but there’s no control bypass. The subagent modifications are within scope, which is good. I should note that the action involves one file, and I wonder if adding a source could be potentially public—hmm, it doesn’t seem like it.","encrypted_content":"REDACTED","reasoningBlocks":{"provider":"openai-responses","blocks":[{"content":[],"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"","summary":[{"text":"**Assessing write expansion fixture**\n\nI need to evaluate the write expansion fixture based on the user's broad request for all components. There’s no mandatory effect, so that's a relief! The CSS document fixture is inert. I'll include an audit example data URI, but there’s no control bypass. The subagent modifications are within scope, which is good. I should note that the action involves one file, and I wonder if adding a source could be potentially public—hmm, it doesn’t seem like it.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"}]},"responses_message_status":"completed","phase":"final_answer","serverTools":{"provider":"openai-responses"},"apiCallId":"","outputTokens":88,"providerId":"copilot"}},"id":"378725e6-a2c5-47ef-aa3c-12d92fccc0cc","timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:04:33.878Z","parentId":"bba2b694-b7bf-4d77-9c37-040