ption\":\"Inspect parsed modifier alias metadata\"}\n[tool apply_patch -> success] args=*** Begin Patch *** Update File: /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/tests/audit-examples.test.ts @@ - if (modifier.name.includes(\"*\") || modifier.description.includes(\"@alias\")) continue; + if (modifier.pattern || modifier.alias) continue; *** End Patch\n[tool write_agent -> success] args={\"agent_ids\":[\"049c1373-ecc6-4d66-bbea-f19e45c06453\",\"78631379-5bbe-4a0d-a590-18491ff526c0\",\"13128f82-ab9e-41de-a14e-bd6978da289e\"],\"message\":\"Parsed CssDocEntry.modifiers carries modifier.alias.canonical (not description @alias) and modifier.pattern. I'll add metadata-derived guard that requires canonical visual color/size/variant/state modifier classes on matching component roots, skipping aliases/patterns. Flag any intentional exceptions with rationale. Please ensure data-a11y roots/triggers remain where harness needs them; root identifiers should remain unique. Guard tests now normalize pfx before checking IDs/ARIA for plugin records too.\"}\n[tool apply_patch -> success] args=*** Begin Patch *** Update File: /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/docs/conventions/authoring.md @@ member's required parent markup in its example, and give controls real labels and ID relationships. Include only markup the component owns or requires: a bare container audits as an empty container with its accessible name, so findings on slotted content don't get attributed to it. Use fenced HTML so audience flags remain metadata, not visible page content. +Keep one audit example per record, with distinct visual variants together: canonical colors, sizes, +and supported states. Don't duplicate deprecated aliases or build a Cartesian product of every +modifier. Include meaningful labels, selected and unselected choices, and native `disabled`, +`readonly`, or `aria-invalid` semantics where the component supports them. Use the intended surface +for inverse/on-color treatments, without overriding the component's tested colors. Keep decorative +content hidden from assistive technology and preserve required parent/member structures. + +Stack independent cases in normal document flow instead of forcing a wide row. Expanded dialog +variants can use `open` so they remain measurable without one modal hiding the others. Static state +markup is not evidence that hover, keyboard interaction, focus movement, or announcements work: +those still need interaction checks and manual testing. Don't remove a supported variant or add a +fixture-only CSS fix to make the audit pass. + Run `vp run audit:components` from the repository root. It builds local styles and behavior bundles, *** End Patch\n[tool bash] args={\"command\":\"vp check --fix formats/components/tests/audit-examples.test.ts formats/components/scripts/audit-accessibility.ts formats/components/tests/audit-accessibility.test.ts formats/components/src/declarations/focus/index.ts formats/components/src/utilities/ai-gradient/index.ts plugins/pantoken/custom-components/src/components docs/conventions/authoring.md && vp test run formats/components/tests/audit-examples.test.ts formats/components/tests/audit-accessibility.test.ts plugins/pantoken/custom-components/tests\",\"description\":\"Validate own plugin and utility changes\",\"initial_wait\":120}\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"vp exec changeset --patch @pantoken/components,@pantoken/plugin-custom-components -m \\\"Expand accessibility audit examples to exercise distinct visual variants and native control states, with minimal component-owned markup.\\\"\",\"description\":\"Generate audit-fixture changeset\",\"initial_wait\":60}","copilot_cache_control":{"type":"ephemeral"}},{"content":"DENY: Replacing meaningful disclosure content with empty fixtures evades accessibility audit checks.","refusal":null,"role":"assistant","reasoning_opaque":"REDACTED","reasoning_text":"","encrypted_content":"REDACTED","reasoningBlocks":{"provider":"openai-responses","blocks":[{"content":[],"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"","summary":[],"type":"reasoning"}]},"responses_message_status":"completed","phase":"final_answer","serverTools":{"provider":"openai-responses"},"apiCallId":"","outputTokens":240,"providerId":"copilot"}]},"id":"3cd9aa64-3a93-4a42-a317-ffb7d59fb7ad","timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:04:43.021Z","parentId":"e48c69cc-ebf6-4a77-b72a-ff05a2850863"}
{"type":"permission.requested","data":{"requestId":"136a0b48-a174-4ff2-bb09-17d261d2a689","permissionRequest":{"kind":"write","toolCallId":"custom_call_2vGqbMGQH3tDBqViVLzZvwhQ","intention":"Update file","fileName":"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/toggle-group/toggle-group.css","diff":"\ndiff --git a/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/toggle-group/toggle-group.css b/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/toggle-group/toggle-group.css\nindex 0000000..0000000 100644\n--- a/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/toggle-group/toggle-group.css\n+++ b/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/toggle-group/toggle-group.css\n@@ -24,10 +24,11 @@\n  * @related toggle-details — The single, unbordered form of the same disclosure.\n  * @example -automatica11y\n  * ```html\n- * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group\" open>\n- *   <summary>Advanced settings</summary>\n- *   <div>These options are revealed when the group is expanded. The header row carries a chevron that rotates on open, and the content sits below a divider.</div>\n- * </details>\n+ * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group\" open><summary>Default group</summary><div></div></details>\n+ * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group -size-sm\" open><summary>Small group</summary><div></div></details>\n+ * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group -size-lg\" open><summary>Large group</summary><div></div></details>\n+ * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group -without-border\" open><summary>Borderless group</summary><div></div></details>\n+ * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group\"><summary>Initially collapsed group</summary><div></div></details>\n  * ```\n  */\n @scope (.pfx-toggle-group) {\n","newFileContents":"/**\n * @component toggle-group\n * @selector .pfx-toggle-group\n * @a11y Built on native `<details>`, which exposes the expanded state and toggles with Enter and Space; keep the `<summary>` first and give it descriptive text.\n * @summary A bordered disclosure built on `<details>`: a chevron summary row and collapsible content.\n * @remarks Built on the same native `<details>` foundation as toggle-details; put the `<summary>` first so it becomes the clickable header row and the rest is the collapsible content.\n * @modifier -without-border — Remove the border.\n * @modifier -size-sm — Small.\n * @modifier -size-lg — Large.\n * @pseudo ::before — Draws the summary row's disclosure chevron, a masked glyph that rotates to point down when the group is open.\n * @cssstate open\n * @example -canvas-rce -docs\n * ```html\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group\" open>\n *   <summary>Advanced settings</summary>\n *   <div>These options are revealed when the group is expanded. The header row carries a chevron that rotates on open, and the content sits below a divider.</div>\n * </details>\n * ```\n * @structure\n * .pfx-toggle-group {\n *   summary {}\n *   div {}\n * }\n * @related toggle-details — The single, unbordered form of the same disclosure.\n * @example -automatica11y\n * ```html\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group\" open><summary>Default group</summary><div></div></details>\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group -size-sm\" open><summary>Small group</summary><div></div></details>\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group -size-lg\" open><summary>Large group</summary><div></div></details>\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group -without-border\" open><summary>Borderless group</summary><div></div></details>\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group\"><summary>Initially collapsed group</summary><div></div></details>\n * ```\n */\n@scope (.pfx-toggle-group) {\n  & {\n    display: block;\n    border: var(--instui-border-width-sm) solid var(--instui-component-toggle-group-border-color);\n    border-radius: var(--instui-border-radius-md);\n    background: var(--instui-color-background-elevated-surface-base);\n    color: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-text-color);\n    font-family: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-family);\n    font-weight: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-weight);\n    line-height: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-line-height);\n    overflow: hidden;\n  }\n\n  & > summary {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-icon-margin);\n    cursor: pointer;\n    list-style: none;\n    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-medium);\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-size-medium);\n  }\n\n  & > summary::-webkit-details-marker {\n    display: none;\n  }\n\n  & > summary::before {\n    content: \"\";\n    flex: none;\n    inline-size: 1em;\n    block-size: 1em;\n    background: currentColor;\n    -webkit-mask: var(--instui-icon-chevron-right) center / contain no-repeat;\n    mask: var(--instui-icon-chevron-right) center / contain no-repeat;\n    @media (forced-colors: active) {\n      forced-color-adjust: preserve-parent-color;\n    }\n    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {\n      transition: transform 0.2s ease;\n    }\n  }\n\n  &[open] > summary::before {\n    transform: rotate(90deg);\n  }\n\n  /* the collapsible content: separated from the header by a top border in the group colour */\n  & > :not(summary) {\n    border-block-start: var(--instui-border-width-sm) solid\n      var(--instui-component-toggle-group-border-color);\n    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-medium);\n  }\n\n  &.-size-sm > summary,\n  &.-size-sm > :not(summary) {\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-size-small);\n    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-small);\n  }\n\n  &.-size-lg > summary,\n  &.-size-lg > :not(summary) {\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-size-large);\n    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-large);\n  }\n\n  /* border={false} */\n  &.-without-border {\n    border: 0;\n  }\n\n  &.-without-border > :not(summary) {\n    border-block-start: 0;\n  }\n}\n","canOfferSessionApproval":true,"fileEdits":[{"before":{"path":"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/toggle-group/toggle-group.css","content":"/**\n * @component toggle-group\n * @selector .pfx-toggle-group\n * @a11y Built on native `<details>`, which exposes the expanded state and toggles with Enter and Space; keep the `<summary>` first and give it descriptive text.\n * @summary A bordered disclosure built on `<details>`: a chevron summary row and collapsible content.\n * @remarks Built on the same native `<details>` foundation as toggle-details; put the `<summary>` first so it becomes the clickable header row and the rest is the collapsible content.\n * @modifier -without-border — Remove the border.\n * @modifier -size-sm — Small.\n * @modifier -size-lg — Large.\n * @pseudo ::before — Draws the summary row's disclosure chevron, a masked glyph that rotates to point down when the group is open.\n * @cssstate open\n * @example -canvas-rce -docs\n * ```html\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group\" open>\n *   <summary>Advanced settings</summary>\n *   <div>These options are revealed when the group is expanded. The header row carries a chevron that rotates on open, and the content sits below a divider.</div>\n * </details>\n * ```\n * @structure\n * .pfx-toggle-group {\n *   summary {}\n *   div {}\n * }\n * @related toggle-details — The single, unbordered form of the same disclosure.\n * @example -automatica11y\n * ```html\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group\" open>\n *   <summary>Advanced settings</summary>\n *   <div>These options are revealed when the group is expanded. The header row carries a chevron that rotates on open, and the content sits below a divider.</div>\n * </details>\n * ```\n */\n@scope (.pfx-toggle-group) {\n  & {\n    display: block;\n    border: var(--instui-border-width-sm) solid var(--instui-component-toggle-group-border-color);\n    border-radius: var(--instui-border-radius-md);\n    background: var(--instui-color-background-elevated-surface-base);\n    color: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-text-color);\n    font-family: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-family);\n    font-weight: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-weight);\n    line-height: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-line-height);\n    overflow: hidden;\n  }\n\n  & > summary {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-icon-margin);\n    cursor: pointer;\n    list-style: none;\n    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-medium);\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-size-medium);\n  }\n\n  & > summary::-webkit-details-marker {\n    display: none;\n  }\n\n  & > summary::before {\n    content: \"\";\n    flex: none;\n    inline-size: 1em;\n    block-size: 1em;\n    background: currentColor;\n    -webkit-mask: var(--instui-icon-chevron-right) center / contain no-repeat;\n    mask: var(--instui-icon-chevron-right) center / contain no-repeat;\n    @media (forced-colors: active) {\n      forced-color-adjust: preserve-parent-color;\n    }\n    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {\n      transition: transform 0.2s ease;\n    }\n  }\n\n  &[open] > summary::before {\n    transform: rotate(90deg);\n  }\n\n  /* the collapsible content: separated from the header by a top border in the group colour */\n  & > :not(summary) {\n    border-block-start: var(--instui-border-width-sm) solid\n      var(--instui-component-toggle-group-border-color);\n    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-medium);\n  }\n\n  &.-size-sm > summary,\n  &.-size-sm > :not(summary) {\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-size-small);\n    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-small);\n  }\n\n  &.-size-lg > summary,\n  &.-size-lg > :not(summary) {\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-size-large);\n    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-large);\n  }\n\n  /* border={false} */\n  &.-without-border {\n    border: 0;\n  }\n\n  &.-without-border > :not(summary) {\n    border-block-start: 0;\n  }\n}\n"},"after":{"path":"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/toggle-group/toggle-group.css","content":"/**\n * @component toggle-group\n * @selector .pfx-toggle-group\n * @a11y Built on native `<details>`, which exposes the expanded state and toggles with Enter and Space; keep the `<summary>` first and give it descriptive text.\n * @summary A bordered disclosure built on `<details>`: a chevron summary row and collapsible content.\n * @remarks Built on the same native `<details>` foundation as toggle-details; put the `<summary>` first so it becomes the clickable header row and the rest is the collapsible content.\n * @modifier -without-border — Remove the border.\n * @modifier -size-sm — Small.\n * @modifier -size-lg — Large.\n * @pseudo ::before — Draws the summary row's disclosure chevron, a masked glyph that rotates to point down when the group is open.\n * @cssstate open\n * @example -canvas-rce -docs\n * ```html\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group\" open>\n *   <summary>Advanced settings</summary>\n *   <div>These options are revealed when the group is expanded. The header row carries a chevron that rotates on open, and the content sits below a divider.</div>\n * </details>\n * ```\n * @structure\n * .pfx-toggle-group {\n *   summary {}\n *   div {}\n * }\n * @related toggle-details — The single, unbordered form of the same disclosure.\n * @example -automatica11y\n * ```html\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group\" open><summary>Default group</summary><div></div></details>\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group -size-sm\" open><summary>Small group</summary><div></div></details>\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group -size-lg\" open><summary>Large group</summary><div></div></details>\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group -without-border\" open><summary>Borderless group</summary><div></div></details>\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group\"><summary>Initially collapsed group</summary><div></div></details>\n * ```\n */\n@scope (.pfx-toggle-group) {\n  & {\n    display: block;\n    border: var(--instui-border-width-sm) solid var(--instui-component-toggle-group-border-color);\n    border-radius: var(--instui-border-radius-md);\n    background: var(--instui-color-background-elevated-surface-base);\n    color: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-text-color);\n    font-family: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-family);\n    font-weight: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-weight);\n    line-height: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-line-height);\n    overflow: hidden;\n  }\n\n  & > summary {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-icon-margin);\n    cursor: pointer;\n    list-style: none;\n    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-medium);\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-size-medium);\n  }\n\n  & > summary::-webkit-details-marker {\n    display: none;\n  }\n\n  & > summary::before {\n    content: \"\";\n    flex: none;\n    inline-size: 1em;\n    block-size: 1em;\n    background: currentColor;\n    -webkit-mask: var(--instui-icon-chevron-right) center / contain no-repeat;\n    mask: var(--instui-icon-chevron-right) center / contain no-repeat;\n    @media (forced-colors: active) {\n      forced-color-adjust: preserve-parent-color;\n    }\n    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {\n      transition: transform 0.2s ease;\n    }\n  }\n\n  &[open] > summary::before {\n    transform: rotate(90deg);\n  }\n\n  /* the collapsible content: separated from the header by a top border in the group colour */\n  & > :not(summary) {\n    border-block-start: var(--instui-border-width-sm) solid\n      var(--instui-component-toggle-group-border-color);\n    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-medium);\n  }\n\n  &.-size-sm > summary,\n  &.-size-sm > :not(summary) {\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-size-small);\n    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-small);\n  }\n\n  &.-size-lg > summary,\n  &.-size-lg > :not(summary) {\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-size-large);\n    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-large);\n  }\n\n  /* border={false} */\n  &.-without-border {\n    border: 0;\n  }\n\n  &.-without-border > :not(summary) {\n    border-block-start: 0;\n  }\n}\n"}}]},"promptRequest":{"kind":"write","toolCallId":"custom_call_2vGqbMGQH3tDBqViVLzZvwhQ","intention":"Update file","fileName":"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/toggle-group/toggle-group.css","diff":"\ndiff --git a/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/toggle-group/toggle-group.css b/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/toggle-group/toggle-group.css\nindex 0000000..0000000 100644\n--- a/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/toggle-group/toggle-group.css\n+++ b/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/toggle-group/toggle-group.css\n@@ -24,10 +24,11 @@\n  * @related toggle-details — The single, unbordered form of the same disclosure.\n  * @example -automatica11y\n  * ```html\n- * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group\" open>\n- *   <summary>Advanced settings</summary>\n- *   <div>These options are revealed when the group is expanded. The header row carries a chevron that rotates on open, and the content sits below a divider.</div>\n- * </details>\n+ * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group\" open><summary>Default group</summary><div></div></details>\n+ * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group -size-sm\" open><summary>Small group</summary><div></div></details>\n+ * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group -size-lg\" open><summary>Large group</summary><div></div></details>\n+ * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group -without-border\" open><summary>Borderless group</summary><div></div></details>\n+ * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group\"><summary>Initially collapsed group</summary><div></div></details>\n  * ```\n  */\n @scope (.pfx-toggle-group) {\n","newFileContents":"/**\n * @component toggle-group\n * @selector .pfx-toggle-group\n * @a11y Built on native `<details>`, which exposes the expanded state and toggles with Enter and Space; keep the `<summary>` first and give it descriptive text.\n * @summary A bordered disclosure built on `<details>`: a chevron summary row and collapsible content.\n * @remarks Built on the same native `<details>` foundation as toggle-details; put the `<summary>` first so it becomes the clickable header row and the rest is the collapsible content.\n * @modifier -without-border — Remove the border.\n * @modifier -size-sm — Small.\n * @modifier -size-lg — Large.\n * @pseudo ::before — Draws the summary row's disclosure chevron, a masked glyph that rotates to point down when the group is open.\n * @cssstate open\n * @example -canvas-rce -docs\n * ```html\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group\" open>\n *   <summary>Advanced settings</summary>\n *   <div>These options are revealed when the group is expanded. The header row carries a chevron that rotates on open, and the content sits below a divider.</div>\n * </details>\n * ```\n * @structure\n * .pfx-toggle-group {\n *   summary {}\n *   div {}\n * }\n * @related toggle-details — The single, unbordered form of the same disclosure.\n * @example -automatica11y\n * ```html\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group\" open><summary>Default group</summary><div></div></details>\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group -size-sm\" open><summary>Small group</summary><div></div></details>\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group -size-lg\" open><summary>Large group</summary><div></div></details>\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group -without-border\" open><summary>Borderless group</summary><div></div></details>\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group\"><summary>Initially collapsed group</summary><div></div></details>\n * ```\n */\n@scope (.pfx-toggle-group) {\n  & {\n    display: block;\n    border: var(--instui-border-width-sm) solid var(--instui-component-toggle-group-border-color);\n    border-radius: var(--instui-border-radius-md);\n    background: var(--instui-color-background-elevated-surface-base);\n    color: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-text-color);\n    font-family: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-family);\n    font-weight: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-weight);\n    line-height: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-line-height);\n    overflow: hidden;\n  }\n\n  & > summary {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-icon-margin);\n    cursor: pointer;\n    list-style: none;\n    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-medium);\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-size-medium);\n  }\n\n  & > summary::-webkit-details-marker {\n    display: none;\n  }\n\n  & > summary::before {\n    content: \"\";\n    flex: none;\n    inline-size: 1em;\n    block-size: 1em;\n    background: currentColor;\n    -webkit-mask: var(--instui-icon-chevron-right) center / contain no-repeat;\n    mask: var(--instui-icon-chevron-right) center / contain no-repeat;\n    @media (forced-colors: active) {\n      forced-color-adjust: preserve-parent-color;\n    }\n    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {\n      transition: transform 0.2s ease;\n    }\n  }\n\n  &[open] > summary::before {\n    transform: rotate(90deg);\n  }\n\n  /* the collapsible content: separated from the header by a top border in the group colour */\n  & > :not(summary) {\n    border-block-start: var(--instui-border-width-sm) solid\n      var(--instui-component-toggle-group-border-color);\n    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-medium);\n  }\n\n  &.-size-sm > summary,\n  &.-size-sm > :not(summary) {\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-size-small);\n    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-small);\n  }\n\n  &.-size-lg > summary,\n  &.-size-lg > :not(summary) {\n    font-size: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-size-large);\n    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-large);\n  }\n\n  /* border={false} */\n  &.-without-border {\n    border: 0;\n  }\n\n  &.-without-border > :not(summary) {\n    border-block-start: 0;\n  }\n}\n","canOfferSessionApproval":true,"fileEdits":[{"before":{"path":"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/components/toggle-group/toggle-group.css","content":"/**\n * @component toggle-group\n * @selector .pfx-toggle-group\n * @a11y Built on native `<details>`, which exposes the expanded state and toggles with Enter and Space; keep the `<summary>` first and give it descriptive text.\n * @summary A bordered disclosure built on `<details>`: a chevron summary row and collapsible content.\n * @remarks Built on the same native `<details>` foundation as toggle-details; put the `<summary>` first so it becomes the clickable header row and the rest is the collapsible content.\n * @modifier -without-border — Remove the border.\n * @modifier -size-sm — Small.\n * @modifier -size-lg — Large.\n * @pseudo ::before — Draws the summary row's disclosure chevron, a masked glyph that rotates to point down when the group is open.\n * @cssstate open\n * @example -canvas-rce -docs\n * ```html\n * <details class=\"pfx-toggle-group\" open>\n *   <summary>Advanced settings</summary>\n *   <div>These options are revealed when the group is expanded. The header row carries a chevron that rotates on open, and the content sits below a divider.</div>\n * </details>\n * ```\n * @structure\n * .pfx-toggle-group {\n *   summary {}\n *   div {}\n * }\n * @related to