Expand color audit fixtures\\\",\\\"agent_type\\\":\\\"general-purpose\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"background\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"color-fixtures\\\",\\\"prompt\\\":\\\"Implement phase 2 only: expand -automatica11y examples for core components button,alert,badge,pill,avatar,text,heading,progress,progress-circle,view,link,close-button,spinner,card,context-view. Own ONLY their source dirs under formats/components/src/components (if record lives elsewhere inspect exact registry and edit only its source). Inspect actual CSS/metadata before edit. Cover all distinct supported colors/sizes/states, dedup aliases; one audit example per record with all variants. Use realistic valid required semantics and minimal owned content, no unrelated components. Inverse/on-color variants require correct contrasting surface, not inline overrides of tested color; inspect tokens/available surface utilities. Keep docs/Canvas examples and runtime CSS unchanged. Don't hide failures or drop difficult variants. Avoid manufacturing reflow from wide fixture layouts. Use apply_patch, follow docs/conventions/authoring.md. Run guard tests if feasible. No commits/snapshot changes. Return paths and coverage decisions. Do not delegate. Other agents own forms/size/plugins; ignore unrelated worktree changes.\\\"}\\n[tool task -> success] args={\\\"description\\\":\\\"Expand structural audit fixtures\\\",\\\"agent_type\\\":\\\"general-purpose\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"background\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"structural-fixtures\\\",\\\"prompt\\\":\\\"Implement phases 3 and core portion of 5: inspect and strengthen all remaining core component audit examples EXCLUDING color agent owned button,alert,badge,pill,avatar,text,heading,progress,progress-circle,view,link,close-button,spinner,card,context-view and forms agent owned text-input,text-area,simple-select,input-group,number-input,checkbox,radio,tag,form-field,form-field-group,radio-input-group,form-field-messages,in-place-edit,file-drop,range-input. Your scope includes list,