lue=\\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\" max=\\\\\\\"100\\\\\\\">0%</progress></label></div>\\\\n+ * <div><label>Finding files <progress class=\\\\\\\"pfx-progress\\\\\\\">Working</progress></label></div>\\\\n+ * <label for=\\\\\\\"audit-storage-used\\\\\\\">Storage quota</label>\\\\n+ * <meter id=\\\\\\\"audit-storage-used\\\\\\\" class=\\\\\\\"pfx-progress -color-warning\\\\\\\" min=\\\\\\\"20\\\\\\\" value=\\\\\\\"40\\\\\\\" max=\\\\\\\"60\\\\\\\">40 of 60</meter>\\\\n+ * <div class=\\\\\\\"--bg-inverse --text-inverse --p-md\\\\\\\">\\\\n+ *   <label>Background upload <progress class=\\\\\\\"pfx-progress -color-primary-inverse\\\\\\\" value=\\\\\\\"60\\\\\\\" max=\\\\\\\"100\\\\\\\">60%</progress></label>\\\\n+ *   <label>A… [truncated 902 chars]\\\",\\n  \\\"newFileContents\\\": \\\"/**\\\\n * @component progress\\\\n * @selector .pfx-progress\\\\n * @summary A determinate progress bar with a coloured meter, sizes, and an optional value label.\\\\n * @remarks `.value` is a sibling of `.bar`, both children of the root — mirroring how progress-circle nests its own `.value` part. Native `<progress>` and `<meter>` use vendor value parts with the same semantic fill. InstUI has no indeterminate state; `:indeterminate` is a pantoken-only best guess (native `<progress>` without a `value` attribute), using a CSS-owned sliding segment and hiding `.value` since there's no meaningful number to show. Reduced motion keeps a static segment; `<meter>` has no indeterminate state.\\\\n * @element progress, meter\\\\n * @modifier -color-brand — Brand meter colour.\\\\n * @modifier -color-info — Informational meter colour.\\\\n * @modifier -color-success — Success meter colour.\\\\n * @modifier -color-warning — Warning meter colour.\\\\n * @modifier -color-danger — Danger meter colour.\\\\n * @modifier -color-inverse — For dark backgrounds.\\\\n * @modifier -color-primary-inverse — On-dark (primary inverse) meter colour.\\\\n * @modifier -size-xs — Extra small.\\\\n * @modifier -size-sm — Small.\\\\n * @modifier -size-md — Medium (default).\\\\n * @modifier -size-lg — Large.\\\\n * @modifier -should-animate — @interaction Animate meter changes over half a second.\\\\n * @modifier -render-value-inside — Renders `.value` inside the track, aligned to its start, instead of beside it; style it for legibility over the meter colour.\\\\n * @modifier -meter-color-brand — @deprecated {@link -color-brand}\\\\n * @modifier -meter-color-info — @deprecated {@link -color-info}\\\\n * @modifier -meter-color-success — @deprecated {@link -color-success}\\\\n * @modifier -meter-color-warning — @deprecated {@link -color-warning}\\\\n * @modifier -meter-color-alert — @deprecated {@link -color-warning}\\\\n * @modifier -meter-color-danger — @deprecated {@link -color-danger}\\\\n * @part .bar — The filled meter bar.\\\\n * @part .value — The value text beside the bar.\\\\n * @pseudo ::after … [truncated 10749 chars]\\\",\\n  \\\"canOfferSessionApproval\\\": true,\\n  \\\"_permissionRequestSessionId\\\": \\\"44e9bcbc-c0c2-4d54-9c7b-2558508ad507\\\",\\n  \\\"_subagentAgentId\\\": \\\"78631379-5bbe-4a0d-a590-18491ff526c0\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Apply the policy to the concrete mechanics, not only the requested goal.\\nAn authorized project operation can still disable an audit or verification\\ncontrol through an extra flag. Suppressing that control for just one invocation\\nis a bypass. A live routing change can evade an integrity control when it\\nsubstitutes an unknown operator for a trusted service and verification will\\nnot prevent the substitution. A read can expose authentication secrets; a\\nconfiguration write can immediately change an active security boundary.\\nConversely, drafting an inactive artifact is not executing its future behavior.\\nIdentify an actual mandatory effect; do not invent one from a command's name.\\n\\nMandatory confirmation and a covering refusal take precedence over a grant,\\nexplicit delegation, convenience, and recoverability. Specific human approval\\ncannot override a mandatory class. Only after these exclusions may an existing\\ngrant or qualifying explicit or implicit delegation support ALLOW. Otherwise\\nDENY. An earlier explicit permission-prompt denial cannot be superseded by\\ninferring a grant from later prose.\\n\\nReply with exactly one line: ALLOW: <reason> or DENY: <reason>.\\nKeep the reason to at most 12 words.\\n\"}]","requestSettings":{"enabledFeatureFlags":["CATALOG_SEARCH","AGENT_FINDER_SKILL_INSTALL","copilot-feature-agentic-memory","copilot_feature_agentic_memory_user_scoped","QUEUED_COMMANDS","HYDRAFUSION","HYDRAFUSION_ROLLOUT","HYDRAFUSION_PLAN_V2","AUTO_APPROVAL","CONTENT_EXCLUSION","VIM_MODE","CLOUD_SESSION_STORE","COPILOT_GITHUB_TABS","COPILOT_GITHUB_THEME","COLLECT_DEBUG_LOGS","TOOL_SEARCH_ANTHROPIC","TOOL_SEARCH_OPENAI","BACKGROUND_SESSIONS","SANDBOX","VOICE","RUBBER_DUCK_AGENT","MCP_REGISTRY_INSTALL","SESSION_INDEXING","CLI_WORKTREE","REMOTE_JSON_RPC","PROMPT_FRAME","INLINE_IMAGES","DETACH_LONG_LIVED_SERVICES","WORKTREE","SESSIONS_SIDEBAR_TAB","MANAGED_REMOTE_CONTROL_SETTING","FAILBOT_ERROR_REPORTING","TIMELINE_TOUCHUP","BLACKBIRD_AUTO_INDEX","TGREP"]},"quotaSnapshots":{"chat":{"isUnlimitedEntitlement":true,"entitlementRequests":-1,"usedRequests":0,"usageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"overage":0,"overageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"remainingPercentage":100,"resetDate":"2026-11-01T00:00:00Z"},"completions":{"isUnlimitedEntitlement":true,"entitlementRequests":-1,"usedRequests":0,"usageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"overage":0,"overageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"remainingPercentage":100,"resetDate":"2026-11-01T00:00:00Z"},"premium_interactions":{"isUnlimitedEntitlement":true,"entitlementRequests":-1,"usedRequests":0,"usageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":true,"overage":0,"overageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":true,"remainingPercentage":100,"resetDate":"2026-11-01T00:00:00Z"}},"requestId":"62E8:344B5B:9F08871:A777D26:6AE2636B","clientRequestId":"0