  <span class=\\\\\\\"controls\\\\\\\"><input class=\\\\\\\"pfx-text-input\\\\\\\" aria-labelledby=\\\\\\\"audit-field-middle-label\\\\\\\"></span>\\\\n+ * </label>\\\\n+ * <p><label class=\\\\\\\"pfx-form-field -inline\\\\\\\">\\\\n+ *   <span class=\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\" id=\\\\\\\"audit-field-inline-label\\\\\\\">Intrinsic field</span>\\\\n+ *   <span class=\\\\\\\"controls\\\\\\\"><input class=\\\\\\\"pfx-text-input\\\\\\\" aria-labelledby=\\\\\\\"audit-field-inline-label\\\\\\\"></span>\\\\n+ * </label></p>\\\\n+ * <label class=\\\\\\\"pfx-form… [truncated 760 chars]\\\",\\n  \\\"newFileContents\\\": \\\"/**\\\\n * @component form-field\\\\n * @summary A form-field wrapper: a label, its controls, and inline, required, or readonly layouts.\\\\n * @remarks An error message stays hidden until the field's control is `:user-invalid` (after the user interacts) or you add the `-invalid` class. Use `-layout-inline` to put the label beside the controls and `-layout-stacked` to put it above. Also sets its own `gap` between the label, controls, and messages; chaining a `-gap-*` spacing utility modifier overrides that built-in value.\\\\n * @remarks Native validation is opt-in: add `data-native-validation` and load `@pantoken/interactions/form-field.iife.js`, or call `initFormField(host, control, error)`. Supply exactly one native control and one error message with a stable, unique ID. The behavior associates the error after blur or a native validation attempt and removes it when corrected; CSS alone doesn't synchronize ARIA.\\\\n * @modifier -inline — Inline layout (shorthand for `-layout-inline`).\\\\n * @modifier -layout-inline — Inline layout: label beside the controls.\\\\n * @modifier -layout-stacked — Stacked layout: label above the controls.\\\\n * @modifier -label-align-start — Start-align the label text.\\\\n * @modifier -label-align-end — End-align the label text.\\\\n * @modifier -invalid — Invalid (error) state.\\\\n * @modifier -readonly — Read-only state.\\\\n * @modifier -v-align-top — Top-align the label with the controls.\\\\n * @modifier -v-align-bottom — Bottom-align the label with the controls.\\\\n * @part .label — The field label.\\\\n * @part .controls — The control area beside or below the label.\\\\n * @pseudo ::after — Renders the decorative required-field asterisk after the label text when the field is required.\\\\n * @accessibility A wrapping `<label>` names the control. When it also contains messages, use `aria-labelledby` to identify just the visible label text and `aria-describedby` for hints. Associate visible validation errors and synchronize `aria-invalid` in application code or with the opt-in native validat… [truncated 7673 chars]\\\",\\n  \\\"canOfferSessionApproval\\\": true,\\n  \\\"_permissionRequestSessionId\\\": \\\"e0a110b6-b8dd-47be-82d5-cb60da15b229\\\",\\n  \\\"_subagentAgentId\\\": \\\"049c1373-ecc6-4d66-bbea-f19e45c06453\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Apply the policy to the concrete mechanics, not only the requested goal.\\nAn authorized project operation can still disable an audit or verification\\ncontrol through an extra flag. Suppressing that control for just one invocation\\nis a bypass. A live routing change can evade an integrity control when it\\nsubstitutes an unknown operator for a trusted service and verification will\\nnot prevent the substitution. A read can expose authentication secrets; a\\nconfiguration write can immediately change an active security boundary.\\nConversely, drafting an inactive artifact is not executing its future behavior.\\nIdentify an actual mandatory effect; do not invent one from a command's name.\\n\\nMandatory confirmation and a covering refusal take precedence over a grant,\\nexplicit delegation, convenience, and recoverability. Specific human approval\\ncannot override a mandatory class. Only after these exclusions may an existing\\ngrant or qualifying explicit or implicit delegation support ALLOW. Otherwise\\nDENY. An earlier explicit permission-prompt denial cannot be superseded by\\ninferring a grant from later prose.\\n\\nReply with exactly one line: ALLOW: <reason> or DENY: <reason>.\\nKeep the reason to at most 12 words.\\n\"}]","requestSettings":{"enabledFeatureFlags":["CATALOG_SEARCH","AGENT_FINDER_SKILL_INSTALL","copilot-feature-agentic-memory","copilot_feature_agentic_memory_user_scoped","QUEUED_COMMANDS","HYDRAFUSION","HYDRAFUSION_ROLLOUT","HYDRAFUSION_PLAN_V2","AUTO_APPROVAL","CONTENT_EXCLUSION","VIM_MODE","CLOUD_SESSION_STORE","COPILOT_GITHUB_TABS","COPILOT_GITHUB_THEME","COLLECT_DEBUG_LOGS","TOOL_SEARCH_ANTHROPIC","TOOL_SEARCH_OPENAI","BACKGROUND_SESSIONS","SANDBOX","VOICE","RUBBER_DUCK_AGENT","MCP_REGISTRY_INSTALL","SESSION_INDEXING","CLI_WORKTREE","REMOTE_JSON_RPC","PROMPT_FRAME","INLINE_IMAGES","DETACH_LONG_LIVED_SERVICES","WORKTREE","SESSIONS_SIDEBAR_TAB","MANAGED_REMOTE_CONTROL_SETTING","FAILBOT_ERROR_REPORTING","TIMELINE_TOUCHUP","BLACKBIRD_AUTO_INDEX","TGREP"]},"quotaSnapshots":{"chat":{"isUnlimitedEntitlement":true,"entitlementRequests":-1,"usedRequests":0,"usageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"overage":0,"overageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"remainingPercentage":100,"resetDate":"2026-11-01T00:00:00Z"},"completions":{"isUnlimitedEntitlement":true,"entitlementRequests":-1,"usedRequests":0,"usageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"overage":0,"overageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"remainingPercentage":100,"resetDate":"2026-11-01T00:00:00Z"},"premium_interactions":{"isUnlimitedEntitlement":true,"entitlementRequests":-1,"usedRequests":0,"usageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":true,"overage":0,"overageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":true,"remainingPercentage":100,"resetDate":"2026-11-01T00:00:00Z"}},"requestId":"5EEB:3AF051:9586E49:9E0387C:6AE2636B","clientRequestId":"00000-0f8dc8d3-54c6-4ac1-aca5-7b40173f05c4","serviceRequestId":"90480504-929e-4775-8496-e4d6e64d47d2","rte":true,"copilotUsage":{"token_details":[{"batch_size":1000000,"cost_per_batch":10000000000,"model":